WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.496 --> 00:00:09.857
Can you guess what the most popular bear is?

2
00:00:11.698 --> 00:00:13.419
It's not the panda or polar bear.

3
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.122
Here's a hint: most children have this bear.

4
00:00:26.387 --> 00:00:26.927
That's right!

5
00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:28.308
It's the teddy bear.

6
00:00:30.068 --> 00:00:31.869
The teddy bear has a special story.

7
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.870
was the nickname of Theodore Roosevelt.

8
00:00:39.591 --> 00:00:42.512
He was the president of the United States many years ago.

9
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:49.034
President Roosevelt enjoyed the outdoors and nature.

10
00:00:51.674 --> 00:00:52.655
He liked to go hunting.

11
00:00:55.735 --> 00:01:00.213
However, on one hunting trip, President Roosevelt did not see any bears.

12
00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:06.137
He was going to give up and go home.

13
00:01:10.019 --> 00:01:12.560
president has to get something," said one man.

14
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.583
"He will feel bad if he doesn't," said another.

15
00:01:17.603 --> 00:01:22.806
"I have an idea," said a third man.

16
00:01:24.707 --> 00:01:26.228
The man told the others his plan.

17
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:34.238
They found an old bear and tied it to a tree.

18
00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:38.261
Then they ran back to the president.

19
00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:42.384
"Mr. President!

20
00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:43.364
I saw a bear!

21
00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:44.565
Follow me, Mr.

22
00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:46.466
President," said one of the men.

23
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.431
He pointed to the tied-up bear.

24
00:01:53.451 --> 00:01:55.893
"Here is the bear!"

25
00:01:55.913 --> 00:01:59.616
"Shoot it, sir," said another man.

26
00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.501
President Roosevelt looked at the bear.

27
00:02:09.622 --> 00:02:11.583
can I kill this helpless animal?"

28
00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:12.963
shouted the president.

29
00:02:15.024 --> 00:02:15.524
"I can't!

30
00:02:15.944 --> 00:02:16.844
I won't kill it!"

31
00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:22.466
A cartoon appeared in the newspaper a few days later.

32
00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:25.587
It showed President Roosevelt and the bear.

33
00:02:27.807 --> 00:02:29.668
The cartoon quickly became famous.

34
00:02:31.828 --> 00:02:33.649
A candy store owner saw the drawing.

35
00:02:36.131 --> 00:02:38.272
He and his wife decided to make a stuffed bear.

36
00:02:40.554 --> 00:02:43.916
They named it Teddy's Bear and displayed it in their store window.

37
00:02:45.777 --> 00:02:47.298
Everyone wanted the stuffed bear.

38
00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.481
It became very popular.

39
00:02:52.762 --> 00:02:55.844
Over time Teddy's Bear became known as the teddy bear.

40
00:02:58.186 --> 00:03:01.568
And now the teddy bear is loved by children all around the world.
